{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1808 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "1223a6dc3082d8c2614cfc0d4bb5214c21d0b47ecda3bee141572d4e84b0db4d" :edb/db-before-t 1807 :edb/db-after-t 1808 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535120 50 #inst "2026-10-08T17:18:06.417Z" 13194139535120 true] [17592186332130 1145 "To solve the Clairaut differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}-7{y}^{′},\n$$\n\nwe start by setting\n$p={y}^{′}.$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation gives\n\n$$\ny=xp-7p.\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & ={(xp-7p)}^{′} \\\\ p & =p+x{p}^{′}-7{p}^{′} \\\\ 0 & ={p}^{′}(x-7)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe product on the right-hand side equals zero, which means at least one of the factors must be zero.\n\nThe general solution of the Clairaut differential equation is obtained if ${p}^{′}=0.$ Then, $p$ is constant, say \n\n$$\np=c.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $p=c$ into $y=xp-7p,$ we get the general solution\n\n$$\ny=cx-7c.\n$$\n\nThis represents a family of straight lines, one line for each constant value of $c.$" 13194139535120 true] [17592186332130 1145 "To solve the Clairaut differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}-7{y}^{′},\n$$\n\nwe start by setting\n$p={y}^{′}.$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation gives\n\n$$\ny=xp-7p.\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & ={(xp-7p)}^{′} \\\\ p & =p+x{p}^{′}-7{p}^{′} \\\\ 0 & ={p}^{′}(x-7)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe product on the right-hand side equals zero, which means at least one of the factors must be zero.\n\nThe general solution of the Clairaut differential equation is obtained if ${p}^{′}=0.$ Then, $p$ is constant, say \n\n$$\np=c.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $p=c$ into $y=xp-7{p}^{′},$ we get the general solution\n\n$$\ny=cx-7c.\n$$\n\nThis represents a family of straight lines, one line for each constant value of $c.$" 13194139535120 false]] :edb/tempids {}}
